Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(edm): refuse an EDM program at the post door; bound
 the spark gap; electrode tool glyph

Review of PR #1131 (needs-rework at 2c1efae9):
- camcraft-ui: ToolKind::Electrode gets an original glyph
  (assets/ui/svg/tool-electrode.svg, rasterised by `cargo xtask icons`),
  Icon::ToolElectrode and its tool_icon arm.
- posting_family::edm_at_post: every writer (post_script_body, the
  per-mount and per-op writers) refuses an op whose setup's machine is a
  wire or sinker EDM by name before any file is written, until #533 /
  #542 ship a dialect. The built-in mill post no longer reaches an EDM.
- motion::sinker check(): a spark gap that puts the tip at or above the
  approach plane, or that is not smaller than the burn below the work
  top, is refused by name - the plunge never feeds upward.
- SinkerParams::model_floor_z doc says what it is: the global bottom.

Refs #541

